 of Western Australia; Nationwide Children's Hospital; Hansa Biopharma; and Duke University. The company was incorporated in 1980 and is headquartered in Cambridge, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Michael E. Severino M.D. | CEO & Director | Age 59","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 835 people. Revenue per employee of $2.6M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 37%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $148K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Sarepta Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.9B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +33% over the past three years and +111% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -66% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $307M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -15.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (25.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 32% below sector me